<BaseLayout title="Process Improvement & Business Operations" current="/process-improvement/" description="Process improvement, SOP leadership, reporting, quality control, workflow improvement, documentation, and selected project services from Richard Allen.">
<section class="page-intro"><div class="container"><div class="eyebrow">Process Improvement & Business Operations</div><h1>Turn scattered work into repeatable, usable systems.</h1><p class="lede">I’m strongest when a process needs to be documented, simplified, coordinated, measured, standardized, or translated into something people can actually use.</p></div></section>

<section class="section impact-section"><div class="container">
  <div class="callout"><strong>Selected proof point:</strong> led and revamped a multi-month Oregon Employment Department SOP initiative encompassing more than 100 procedures.</div>
  <div class="process-flow" aria-label="Process improvement approach">
    <div class="flow-step"><span>1</span><strong>Understand</strong><small>How the work actually happens</small></div>
    <div class="flow-arrow">→</div>
    <div class="flow-step"><span>2</span><strong>Organize</strong><small>People, steps, inputs, and decisions</small></div>
    <div class="flow-arrow">→</div>
    <div class="flow-step"><span>3</span><strong>Document</strong><small>Clear instructions people can follow</small></div>
    <div class="flow-arrow">→</div>
    <div class="flow-step"><span>4</span><strong>Improve</strong><small>Reduce friction and make work repeatable</small></div>
  </div>
</div></section>

<section class="section"><div class="container">
  <div class="grid two value-grid">
    <article class="card accent-teal"><div class="card-icon">SOP</div><h3>SOP standardization</h3><p>Led and revamped a multi-month initiative encompassing 100+ procedures, helping organize, document, and standardize operational work while supporting training and continuous improvement.</p></article>
    <article class="card accent-blue"><div class="card-icon">QA</div><h3>Quality & process control</h3><p>At HawkSoft, investigated an employee-quality issue involving call and voicemail handling. The work helped management revise QA scoring policy and strengthen process control.</p></article>
    <article class="card accent-gold"><div class="card-icon">KPI</div><h3>Reporting for better decisions</h3><p>Created operational and management reporting from support and call data, including cleaning large Excel exports and turning them into pivot- and KPI-style reporting for leadership.</p></article>
    <article class="card accent-violet"><div class="card-icon">400+</div><h3>Workforce reporting at scale</h3><p>At Oregon Health Authority, managed 400+ position records and maintained 20+ recurring and ad-hoc workforce reports while coordinating with Recruiting, HR, Classification & Compensation, Budget, DEI, and leadership.</p></article>
    <article class="card accent-blue"><div class="card-icon">↻</div><h3>Change & release support</h3><p>Supported major HawkSoft software releases through advance communication, recurring developer/support coordination, launch coverage, and continued training for customers and staff.</p></article>
    <article class="card accent-teal"><div class="card-icon">CX</div><h3>Customer experience systems</h3><p>At The Kotter Group, established and managed a Customer Experience function, maintained client relationships, gathered customer feedback, and created training documentation, presentations, webinars, online content, and customer communications.</p></article>
    <article class="card accent-gold"><div class="card-icon">AUD</div><h3>Accuracy in changing environments</h3><p>Audited hundreds of Pandemic Unemployment Assistance applications while guidance changed rapidly, using tracking and research tools and contributing to training and onboarding materials.</p></article>
    <article class="card accent-violet"><div class="card-icon">16+</div><h3>Supply & warehouse operations</h3><p>At Aramark Foodservice, managed a warehouse team of 16+ and six-figure weekly inventory while overseeing procurement, receiving, storage, distribution, sanitation, shipping, and driver/small-fleet activity.</p></article>
  </div>
</div></section>

<section class="section project-services"><div class="container">
  <div class="section-heading-row"><div><div class="eyebrow">Available for selected project work</div><h2>SOP & process documentation</h2></div><p class="section-note">A practical short-term service for small businesses and teams that need important work documented clearly.</p></div>
  <div class="project-service-panel">
    <div>
      <p class="project-service-lede">If an important process is undocumented, inconsistent, outdated, or mostly living in someone’s head, I can help turn it into clear instructions your team can actually use.</p>
      <div class="service-grid">
        <div><strong>Standard Operating Procedures</strong><span>New SOPs built from notes, screenshots, forms, or existing materials.</span></div>
        <div><strong>Workflow Documentation</strong><span>Clear descriptions of who does what, when, with which inputs and handoffs.</span></div>
        <div><strong>Training & Onboarding Guides</strong><span>Practical documentation that helps people learn and repeat the work consistently.</span></div>
        <div><strong>Existing SOP Cleanup</strong><span>Improve clarity, consistency, organization, usability, and missing or confusing steps.</span></div>
        <div><strong>Customer-Support Procedures</strong><span>Escalation, service, troubleshooting, and support-process documentation.</span></div>
        <div><strong>Process-Gap Identification</strong><span>Surface unclear steps, dependencies, handoff problems, and documentation gaps.</span></div>
      </div>
    </div>
